<h2 id="conclusion">Conclusion</h2>
<p>By using eager loading you can improve your application performance. Sometimes as your application grows, even eager loading is not enough to keep up top performance. In the next tutorial I’ll show you how you can decorate repositories to cache the queries for better performance.</p></article></div><div class="hidden pt-32 min-[1152px]:block"><aside class="sticky top-24 max-h-[calc(100vh-7rem)] overflow-y-auto pb-6"><nav aria-label="On this page"><p class="mb-3 border-b pb-3 font-mono text-xs tracking-wider text-muted-foreground uppercase">On this page</p><ol class="space-y-px"><li><a href="using-repository-pattern-in-laravel-5-eloquent-relations-and-eager-loading#preface" class="block border-l-2 py-1 pl-3 text-sm leading-snug transition-colors hover:text-primary border-transparent text-muted-foreground">Preface</a></li><li><a href="using-repository-pattern-in-laravel-5-eloquent-relations-and-eager-loading#what-is-eager-loading" class="block border-l-2 py-1 pl-3 text-sm leading-snug transition-colors hover:text-primary border-transparent text-muted-foreground">What Is Eager Loading?</a></li><li><a href="using-repository-pattern-in-laravel-5-eloquent-relations-and-eager-loading#extending-repository-class" class="block border-l-2 py-1 pl-3 text-sm leading-snug transition-colors hover:text-primary border-transparent text-muted-foreground">Extending Repository Class</a></li><li><a href="using-repository-pattern-in-laravel-5-eloquent-relations-and-eager-loading#conclusion" class="block border-l-2 py-1 pl-3 text-sm leading-snug transition-colors hover:text-primary border-transparent text-muted-foreground">Conclusion</a></li></ol></nav><section aria-label="Related service" class="mt-10"><p class="mb-3 border-b pb-3 font-mono text-xs tracking-wider text-muted-foreground uppercase">Related service</p><a class="block leading-snug transition-colors hover:text-primary" href="../architecture-review">Architecture review</a><p class="mt-1 text-sm text-muted-foreground">System b