 what DB you use, how powerful your server is it will always reach the tipping point where your powerful hardware will no longer be your ally. You can try to improve performance by caching these queries, using Redis for example. And it will work just fine, but just temporarily. That way you only delay the inevitable end, which will cost you a lot of money, time and probably you\\u2019ll lose some client(s) or your userbase will be reduced significantly.\"]}),`\n`,(0,s.jsxs)(a.p,{children:[\"Here eager loading come to rescue. Using \",(0,s.jsx)(a.a,{href:\"http://laravel.com/docs/4.2/eloquent#eager-loading\",title:\"Eager Loading\",children:\"eager loading\"}),\" in Laravel is pretty simple. The relations you want to be eager loaded you specify in the with method:\"]}),`\n`,(0,s.jsx)(p,{children:(0,s.jsx)(l,{language:\"php\",code:\"$stores = Store::with('member','products')->get();\",highlightedCode:`\x3Cpre class=\"shiki custom\" style=\"background-color:var(--shiki-background);color:var(--shiki-foreground)\" tabindex=\"0\">\x3Ccode>\x3Cspan class=\"line\">\x3Cspan class=\"hl-fg\">$stores \x3C/span>\x3Cspan class=\"hl-k\">=\x3C/span>\x3Cspan class=\"hl-c\"> Store\x3C/span>\x3Cspan class=\"hl-k\">::\x3C/span>\x3Cspan class=\"hl-f\">with\x3C/span>\x3Cspan class=\"hl-p\">(\x3C/span>\x3Cspan class=\"hl-se\">'member'\x3C/span>\x3Cspan class=\"hl-p\">,\x3C/span>\x3Cspan class=\"hl-se\">'products'\x3C/span>\x3Cspan class=\"hl-p\">)\x3C/span>\x3Cspan class=\"hl-k\">->\x3C/span>\x3Cspan class=\"hl-f\">get\x3C/span>\x3Cspan class=\"hl-p\">()\x3C/span>\x3Cspan class=\"hl-fg\">;\x3C/span>\x3C/span>\x3C/code>\x3C/pre>`,children:\"$stores = Store::with('member','products')->get();\"})}),`\n`,(0,s.jsx)(a.p,{children:\"Now, instead executing 7 queries, by using eager loading we reduced number of queries to just 3:\"}),`\n`,(0,s.jsx)(e,{src:\"https://media.bosnadev.com/hub/1ae8293f9196f309/2015-03-n-plus-one-problem-eager-736x128.webp\",alt:\"N Plus One Problem\",width:736,height:12